---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

const title = 'How OpenCoven works · Local authority, durable continuity';
const description = 'How Coven coordinates local agent work through shared claims, guarded writes, durable records, and principal-approved authority.';
---

<SiteLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/how-it-works">
  <section class="site-shell hero" id="top">
    <div class="hero__copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Current runtime behavior</p>
      <h1>Coordinate agent work without handing away authority.</h1>
      <p class="hero__lede">Coven sits beside the agent harnesses you already use. It keeps shared project intent, claims, guarded writes, and durable evidence legible across sessions while the principal remains the authority boundary.</p>
      <div class="button-row">
        <a class="action action--primary" data-oc-primitive="action" data-oc-state="idle" href="/quickstart">Start locally</a>
        <a class="action" data-oc-primitive="action" data-oc-state="idle" href="/protocol">See the protocol model</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="evidence-card">
      <span class="status status--available" data-oc-primitive="status-indicator" data-oc-state="success">Current Coven runtime</span>
      <h2 class="card-heading">What this page claims</h2>
      <p class="muted">Only behavior represented by the current local runtime and checked-in product truth. Cross-device, hosted, and broader protocol continuity remain maturity-scoped elsewhere.</p>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="flow-heading">
    <div class="site-shell">
      <div class="band__intro"><h2 id="flow-heading">A bounded coordination loop.</h2><p>The runtime turns overlapping agent work into inspectable state rather than hidden convention.</p></div>
      <ol class="proof-sequence" aria-label="Coven coordination flow">
        <li class="proof-step"><div class="proof-step__body"><h3>Sessions declare intent.</h3><p>Each session works through the harness it already uses while Coven records the shared project boundary and intended surface.</p></div></li>
        <li class="proof-step"><div class="proof-step__body"><h3>Claims make overlap explicit.</h3><p>When work touches protected or contested surfaces, ownership and contention become visible instead of being inferred from chat history.</p></div></li>
        <li class="proof-step"><div class="proof-step__body"><h3>Guards hold unsafe mutation.</h3><p>A conflicting write can degrade to a proposal or wait for principal approval rather than silently winning a race.</p></div></li>
        <li class="proof-step"><div class="proof-step__body"><h3>Evidence survives the session.</h3><p>Durable project records preserve what happened, why it happened, and which authority allowed it.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="boundary-heading">
    <div class="site-shell">
      <div class="band__intro"><h2 id="boundary-heading">The boundaries matter.</h2><p>OpenCoven separates identity, authority, orchestration, runtime coordination, and product presentation instead of making one surface own all semantics.</p></div>
      <div class="concept-grid">
        <article class="concept-card"><h3>Identity</h3><p>The governed familiar self and principal binding are not created by a marketing page or orchestration session.</p></article>
        <article class="concept-card"><h3>Authority</h3><p>Protected mutation stays under explicit principal and runtime authority rather than becoming implicit agent permission.</p></article>
        <article class="concept-card"><h3>Continuity</h3><p>Continuity preserves authorized context across work; it is not a claim that every surface or device is already fully synchronized.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
